<%# The accessibility statement of this site (CCS-148). PLACEHOLDER WORDING until the University approves it: the marked notice stays on the page until then. %>
<% content_for :body_class, "page-help" %>
<% content_for :title, "Accessibility of Collections Navigator — University of Melbourne" %>
<%= render NexusCcs::PageBreadcrumbsComponent.new(trail: [ [ "Accessibility", nil ] ]) %>
<%= render NexusCcs::PageBannerComponent.new(title: "Accessibility of Collections Navigator", description: "How accessible this site is, what we check, and how to tell us about a problem.") %>
<main class="help-main-content help-main-content--topic" id="main-content">
<div class="help-layout">
<nav class="jump-nav" aria-labelledby="jump-nav-title" data-controller="jump-nav">
  <div class="jump-nav__container">
    <p class="jump-nav__title" id="jump-nav-title">On this page</p>
    <ul class="jump-nav__list">
      <li class="jump-nav__item"><a class="jump-nav__link" data-jump-nav-target="link" href="#our-aim">Our aim</a></li>
      <li class="jump-nav__item"><a class="jump-nav__link" data-jump-nav-target="link" href="#how-we-check">How we check</a></li>
      <li class="jump-nav__item"><a class="jump-nav__link" data-jump-nav-target="link" href="#known-limits">Known limits</a></li>
      <li class="jump-nav__item"><a class="jump-nav__link" data-jump-nav-target="link" href="#report-a-problem">Report a problem</a></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</nav>
<div class="help-layout__content">
<div class="placeholder-notice" role="note" id="placeholder-notice">
  <p><strong>Placeholder wording, not yet approved.</strong> The University must approve this statement, including the conformance claim, before it is relied on. Until then it describes only what the development team has checked.</p>
</div>

<section class="help-section" id="our-aim" aria-labelledby="h-our-aim">
  <header class="help-section__header">
    <h2 class="help-section__heading" id="h-our-aim">Our aim</h2>
  </header>
  <ul class="help-section__items">
    <li class="help-section__item">
      <p class="help-section__text">Collections Navigator is designed to meet the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2, level AA. We have not had the site independently audited, so we do not claim that it fully conforms. For the University's own accessibility commitments, see <a href="https://www.unimelb.edu.au/accessibility">the University of Melbourne accessibility page</a>.</p>
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="help-section" id="how-we-check" aria-labelledby="h-how-we-check">
  <header class="help-section__header">
    <h2 class="help-section__heading" id="h-how-we-check">How we check</h2>
  </header>
  <ul class="help-section__items">
    <li class="help-section__item">
      <p class="help-section__text">Every change to the site is checked automatically with an accessibility testing tool (axe-core) against the main pages, the search results, a record page and the pop-up windows. Automatic tools find only some problems. Checking with a keyboard and a screen reader is done by people, and is not yet done for every page.</p>
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="help-section" id="known-limits" aria-labelledby="h-known-limits">
  <header class="help-section__header">
    <h2 class="help-section__heading" id="h-known-limits">Known limits</h2>
  </header>
  <ul class="help-section__items">
    <li class="help-section__item">
      <p class="help-section__text">Descriptions of collection items, and the text of their images, come from the collection teams' catalogue records. Many records have no description of the image, and some use older words that are no longer appropriate. See <a href="<%= help_path(anchor: "indigenous") %>">Indigenous cultural data and access</a>.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="help-section__item">
      <p class="help-section__text">Scanned documents, audio and video held by the collections may not have a transcript or captions yet. Ask the collection team if you need one.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="help-section__item">
      <p class="help-section__text">The image viewer on a record page can be used with a keyboard, but zooming and moving a large image is easier with a mouse or touch screen.</p>
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="help-section" id="report-a-problem" aria-labelledby="h-report-a-problem">
  <header class="help-section__header">
    <h2 class="help-section__heading" id="h-report-a-problem">Report a problem</h2>
  </header>
  <ul class="help-section__items">
    <li class="help-section__item">
      <p class="help-section__text">If you cannot use part of this site, or you need a collection item in another format, tell us on the <a href="<%= help_path(anchor: "contact-us") %>">Contact us</a> section of Help. Say which page you were on and what got in your way. <span data-placeholder>[Placeholder: the University to state how quickly it will reply, and the complaint route if a reply does not fix the problem.]</span></p>
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>
</div>
</div>
</main>
